  "version": "0.6.1-beta.3",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.6.1-beta.2`\n\n### Fixes\n\n- turn mouse reporting off once the shell is back at its prompt, since a program killed before it could turn reporting off (Ctrl+C while claude starts) left every mouse move typed into the shell's line editor as text like 35;74;19M: a shell integration prompt mark (OSC 133/633 A) turns it off at once, and on macOS and Linux local tabs, which have no marks by default, the new pty_shell_in_foreground command is asked once output settles whether the shell leads the terminal's foreground process group again, checking the leader is still a shell so an exec'd tmux keeps its reporting ([44361ad0](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/44361ad084abf2955262c80d9ac4bfcaed137b60))\n- let the settings sidebar scroll when the dialog is too short to show every category, since the aside had no overflow and the categories below the fold were clipped out of reach ([e3e3a63c](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/e3e3a63cfcc2427516586f5a33027a64ccd698e2))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.6.1-beta.2...v0.6.1-beta.3](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.6.1-beta.2...v0.6.1-beta.3)",
